---
date added: 2026-10-13
title: Rigatoni With White Bolognese
author: Amanda Hesser
source: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11111-rigatoni-with-white-bolognese
tags: pasta, dinner, beef, pork
servings: 4
time required: 1 hour
---

Add enough @extra virgin olive oil{} to a large, deep #sauté pan{} to coat the base and place over medium-high heat. When the oil shimmers, add the @sweet onion{1/2} (peeled and finely chopped), @carrots{2%medium} (peeled and finely chopped) and @celery{1%stalk} (finely chopped) and sauté until glassy and just tender, about ~{5%minutes}. Season lightly with @sea salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{}. Add the @mild Italian pork sausage meat{1%pound} (removed from casings) and @ground beef{1%pound} (not lean) to the pan, breaking it into walnut-size pieces, and brown well.

Pour in the @dry Italian white wine{1 1/2%cups} and keep at a rapid simmer until the pan is almost dry. Then pour in 1 ½ cups of the @beef bouillon{1%cube} (dissolved in 2 cups simmering water) and lower the heat to medium. Simmer gently, uncovered, until the bouillon is nearly gone, stirring now and then. Meanwhile, chop the rehydrated @dried porcini mushrooms{1 1/2%ounces} (rehydrated in 3 cups lukewarm water) into small pieces, reserving the liquid.

Bring a large #pot{} of salted water to a boil. Add mushroom liquid to the sauce to cover the meat halfway (about 1 cup) along with the porcini and continue simmering until the sauce is loose but not soupy, about ~{10%minutes}. Taste and adjust salt and pepper; it should be highly seasoned. When the consistency is right, fold the @heavy cream{1/3%cup} in. Remove from the heat and cover.

When the pasta water is at a full boil, add the @rigatoni{1%pound} and cook until still firm, but not hard, in the center. When the pasta is almost done, scoop out 1 cup of pasta water and reserve. Drain the pasta and then return it to the &pot{}. Pour the pasta sauce on top and fold in with a #wooden spoon{}. The pasta should not be dry. Add a little pasta water or mushroom liquid to loosen it. (It will continue to soak up sauce on the way to the table.) Serve in one large bowl or in individual bowls, passing the @freshly grated Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese{3/4%cup} at the table.
